## Script Standards (this repo)

Setup scripts (`scripts/setup-*.sh/.ps1`) must follow these conventions.

### Block order

**Bash:** shebang/header > `set -euo pipefail` > logging block (`ERRORS=0` + helpers) > OS guard > body > exit footer
**PS1:** header > logging block (`$errors = 0` + helpers) > OS guard > body > exit footer

### Error tracking (required)

- `log_error()` MUST do `ERRORS=$((ERRORS + 1))`
- `LogError` MUST do `$script:errors++`
- Missing tracking is a bug -- scripts silently exit 0 on failure.

### Logging helpers

Bash: `log`/`log_ok`/`log_error`/`log_warn`. PS1: `Log`/`LogOk`/`LogError`/`LogWarn`. UTC timestamps with Z suffix.

### Exit footer

Check error counter, exit 1 on failure, exit 0 on success. See gold standards: `scripts/setup-user-mcp.sh/.ps1`.
